# Taste profile v1

## What makes an article good

I want articles that tackle a subject through more than one lens. Not a pure
finance article; not a pure AI article. An AI piece that takes the financial
consequences seriously, or a finance piece that incorporates the geopolitical
context — and in both cases the additional context has to do actual work.

The test is interaction, not coverage: the second domain must change the
conclusion about the first. An article that explains how export controls drive
margin compression is doing this. An article that mentions AI and also mentions
markets is not.

Argument backed by evidence — numbers, mechanisms, named specifics — is what I
value. Strong opinions are fine, provided they are argued.

## What makes an article bad

- Coverage centred on a person or a personality rather than on a mechanism.
- Assertion without support: punditry, vibes, "here's my take".
- A subject treated from a single perspective, however well.
- Breadth by aggregation — link roundups and grab-bags that touch many domains
  without any of them bearing on another.
